_site/
.quarto/
# _freeze/ is COMMITTED on purpose. Notebooks are executed on your machine by
# `make all`, inspected, and the frozen output is what publishes -- so CI needs
# only Quarto, not R and not SciPy. Run `make all` and commit _freeze/ with the
# lesson it belongs to. See LOCAL.md.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.Rproj.user/
.Rhistory
.RData
.venv/
# generated data, incl. the RAG corpus — rebuild with `make rag-build`
data/derived/
.DS_Store

/.quarto/

# never commit papers — see CONTRIBUTING.md
*.pdf
*.epub

# personal library — links page and PDFs stay local
reading/papers/*
!reading/papers/README.md
_to_delete/

# raw openFDA responses — regenerate with `make fda`, never committed
fda-cache/
